  "narrative": "No assessments are due, and voluntary validation capacity is exhausted, so this explore step registers discovery comparisons only. The central unresolved scientific issue is not whether feature_063 has an overall lower-outcome association, which is supported and independently validated, but how much its association depends on measured context after removing correlated dominant markers. I therefore register focused feature_063 mean-difference tests in a second large categorical context, feature_046 level_002, and in upper and lower quartile backgrounds of feature_049, each within a core-negative eligible population excluding feature_037, feature_002, and feature_010. The hypothesis is that a robust lower-outcome feature_063 association should persist in these contexts; plausible alternatives are attenuation or null because of predictor correlation, sparse exposed cells, or context specificity. I also register a feature_049 upper-versus-complement interaction in the same core-negative population. This asks whether feature_049 is a credible modifier of the feature_063 lower-outcome effect rather than merely providing two separate strata; expected direction is uncertain because no interaction claim has previously been supported. For feature_003, which is near but below the threshold overall and in cleaner contexts, I register a core-negative test without excluding feature_063, a larger population than H233, to test whether its lower-outcome near-threshold effect can become clearer once correlated core markers are removed. I also test feature_003 within feature_063=1 to examine whether it contributes independently or disappears when the feature_063-positive background is fixed. For the core accepted predictors, I register pair-background and high-feature_019 main-effect tests: feature_002 among feature_037=0 and feature_010=1, feature_010 among feature_037=0 and feature_002=1, and feature_002/feature_010 in high feature_019 backgrounds excluding the other core predictors. These test independent persistence and reduce apparent collinearity among the dominant binary predictors, but they do not establish causality or transportability. All proposed comparisons are observational Welch contrasts in the supplied dataset. For lower-outcome claims direction=-1, a positive returned estimate means raw outcome_001 is lower in exposed than comparator; for higher-outcome claims direction=1, a positive returned estimate means raw outcome_001 is higher in exposed. Any new claim is provisional and must clear the 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold in the registered direction with adequately sized cells.",
  "research_notes": "Current supported dataset-specific associations: feature_037 lower outcome_001; feature_002 higher; feature_010 higher; feature_063 lower overall, with selected context persistence and validation. No interaction claim has been accepted. Nominal markers feature_007, feature_058, feature_015 and many low-prevalence binaries remain negative. Main uncertainty: conditional specificity of feature_063, especially after controlling correlated core markers; feature_003 is near-threshold but unresolved. Validation capacity is exhausted. Iteration 20 plan: register focused discovery tests of feature_063 persistence in feature_046 level_002 and feature_049 quartile backgrounds after removing feature_037, feature_002, and feature_010; test a feature_063-by-feature_049 interaction in that core-negative population; test feature_003 core-negative without excluding feature_063 and feature_003 within feature_063=1; test core pair/age-context persistence for feature_002 and feature_010. Do not promote low-prevalence or opportunistic contrasts unless they clear the 0.15 threshold with adequate cells. Interpret signed estimates exactly as displayed; all conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
}

