  "narrative": "No assessments are due and voluntary validation capacity is exhausted, so this step registers discovery comparisons only. The two highest-value remaining scientific questions are: (1) whether feature_003's persistent lower-outcome near-threshold signal can reach the 0.15 threshold once its overlap with other predictors is reduced, and (2) how much of feature_063's accepted lower-outcome association is robust across measured contexts versus context-specific or artifactually induced by correlated dominant markers. For feature_003, I test feature_003=1 versus 0 within feature_063=0 to remove a lower-outcome predictor that may mask or amplify the effect, then within a core-negative population additionally requiring feature_037=0, feature_002=0, feature_010=0, and feature_063=0. If feature_003 is a genuine lower-outcome marker, these signed lower-outcome contrasts should remain positive and exceed threshold; if it is mainly correlated with accepted markers or is a subthreshold fluctuation, they should remain near or below threshold. I also register a feature_003-by-feature_063 interaction to test whether feature_003 acts more strongly in feature_063-positive versus feature_063-negative backgrounds; this is expected to be uncertain and requires adequate four-cell support. For feature_063, I move away from extremely sparse post-hoc strata and test larger feature_049 quartile contexts without excluding core markers, because the prior low-feature_049 context was accepted but had only 35 exposed observations, whereas the high-feature_049 core-negative context was unresolved. These tests ask whether low-feature_049 marks a robust lower-outcome context and whether high-feature_049 attenuates the association. A larger feature_063-by-feature_049 interaction tests effect modification more directly than separate strata. I also test feature_063 in a middle feature_040 range within the core-negative population, in core-negative feature_003=0, and in core-negative high feature_019; these are selected to preserve adequate cells while probing whether feature_063's association persists after removing dominant correlated predictors or in a clinically interpretable numeric background. Plausible alternatives for all feature_063 comparisons are attenuation to null, threshold-limited effects, or unstable small-cell estimates. All proposed analyses remain dataset-specific observational Welch contrasts and do not imply causality, unique biological roles, or transportability.",
